From 480e72471ec3f9f64833bfbb925a1d67d3711ce6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: davide marchetto <dvdmarchetto@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:39:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Process same-time events in scheduler order on a single
 thread

The single-threaded executor stored its work queue in a `Vec` and popped
the last task first, so same-time events scheduled by different models
were processed in reverse scheduler-key order, i.e. by descending origin
model. The scheduler queue itself is ordered by (time, origin) since
#62/#122 for the sake of determinism; the LIFO work queue reversed that
order on a single thread, the configuration in which determinism is
achievable.

The work queue is now a `VecDeque` used in FIFO order. A test checks
the processing order of same-time events from five models on one thread
(it fails with the former LIFO queue: [4, 3, 2, 1, 0]), and the
"Message ordering guarantees" section documents the single-threaded
order.
